# Exclude development-only material from the packaged release.
# drupal.org builds release tarballs with `git archive`, which honors
# export-ignore. These paths stay in the git repo but are not shipped to a
# site installing from a release.
#
# CHANGELOG.md and README.md are deliberately NOT listed: both are useful to
# someone who has installed the module, which is the test for whether a file
# belongs in the tarball.
# Test suite: wanted in the repo and by CI, not by a running site.
# Tooling config: consumed by CI and local development, not by a site.
/.gitattributes export-ignore
/.gitignore export-ignore

# WHAT STAYS IN THE TARBALL, and why these four lines were removed.
#
# Measured 2026-09-06 against the packaged releases installed on this machine —
# ai, paragraphs, entity_reference_revisions, field_group, webform, token,
# pathauto:
#
#   tests/            7 of 7 ship them. Excluding them means nobody can run
#                     this module's tests from a release, and webform's own
#                     attempt to exclude tests was closed `won't fix` upstream.
#   .gitlab-ci.yml    7 of 7 ship it.
#   phpcs.xml.dist    the ruleset is self-contained, and shipping it is what
#   phpstan.neon      makes `composer phpcs` / `composer phpstan` work INSIDE
#                     an extracted package — the check apex's S4-I calls for
#                     and the one thing a symlinked test can never prove.
#
# `export-ignore` only affects the archive; every local run and CI job sees
# these files either way.
